.TH SDL_GetCurrentTime 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetCurrentTime \- Gets the current value of the system realtime clock in nanoseconds since Jan 1, 1970 in Universal Coordinated Time (UTC).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_time.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_GetCurrentTime(SDL_Time *ticks);
.fi
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I ticks
the
.BR SDL_Time
to hold the returned tick count\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

